WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.208 --> 00:00:01.793
The world is saying goodbye

00:00:01.793 --> 00:00:03.044
to a beloved actor

00:00:03.044 --> 00:00:05.296
and one of our best friends.

00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:06.506
Matthew Perry

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.049
was just 54 years old

00:00:08.049 --> 00:00:10.093
when he died at his Los Angeles home.

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:11.344
On Saturday.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.722
He was found unresponsive in his hot tub,

00:00:14.055 --> 00:00:15.015
and the cause of death

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.558
is still unknown, pending

00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:18.560
toxicology testing.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:19.686
Perry was best known

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:20.186
for playing

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.938
Chandler Bing on the beloved

00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:23.648
sitcom Friends.

00:00:23.648 --> 00:00:24.941
And tonight, his costars

00:00:24.941 --> 00:00:26.860
releasing a statement saying,

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.821
We are all so utterly devastated

00:00:29.821 --> 00:00:31.573
by the loss of Matthew.

00:00:31.573 --> 00:00:34.034
We were more than just cast mates.

00:00:34.451 --> 00:00:36.661
We are a family.

00:00:36.661 --> 00:00:38.913
There is so much to say.

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:40.665
But right now, we're going

00:00:40.665 --> 00:00:41.458
to take a moment

00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:42.250
to grieve

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.670
and process this unfathomable loss.

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:48.048
My next guest is executive

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:50.717
producer of Friends Kevin Bright.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:51.593
Kevin,

00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:52.093
thank you

00:00:52.093 --> 00:00:54.471
so much for joining us this evening.

00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:55.263
It is

00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:57.432
unbelievably sad news

00:00:57.432 --> 00:00:58.933
to think about the loss of someone

00:00:58.933 --> 00:01:00.310
that so many of us feel like

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:01.603
we knew personally

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:02.145
watching him

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:04.147
for the better part of three decades.

00:01:04.189 --> 00:01:06.191
I mean, we knew Chandler Bing,

00:01:06.816 --> 00:01:09.360
but you knew Matthew Perry

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:10.862
And I'm wondering

00:01:10.862 --> 00:01:12.155
if you can reflect a little bit

00:01:12.155 --> 00:01:15.575
about what his loss means to you tonight.

00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:20.705
Laura, thanks for having me.

00:01:20.705 --> 00:01:23.666
It's obviously very tragic

00:01:23.666 --> 00:01:26.544
that Matthew's life should end the 64

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:29.798
and especially at a point in his life

00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:31.966
where he seemed to have conquered

00:01:31.966 --> 00:01:34.302
the demons that plagued him for so long.

00:01:34.844 --> 00:01:38.098
And he was on a mission to help people.

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:40.141
And that's what he was focused

00:01:40.141 --> 00:01:41.643
on, I know,

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:45.313
speaking to him a few months before.

00:01:45.313 --> 00:01:47.190
The last time you spoke to him,

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.192
did he seem like he was happy

00:01:49.192 --> 00:01:53.113
and and in good spirits?

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:53.863
Oh, yeah.

00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:55.031
No, he was very up.

00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:59.619
He was very much invested in the projects

00:01:59.994 --> 00:02:01.287
in terms of the direction

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.497
that he was pursuing

00:02:02.497 --> 00:02:06.459
and also was looking to

00:02:06.668 --> 00:02:07.877
make movies again.

00:02:07.877 --> 00:02:10.130
So he was very out.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:11.256
I mean, you've known him since

00:02:11.256 --> 00:02:11.631
he was what?

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:12.841
I mean, 24 years.

00:02:12.841 --> 00:02:14.592
I forget he was 24 years old

00:02:14.592 --> 00:02:15.677
when he started on Friends.

00:02:15.677 --> 00:02:18.012
And you just forget how young he was

00:02:18.012 --> 00:02:19.722
because so many of us are watching it

00:02:19.722 --> 00:02:20.723
in real time right now.

00:02:20.723 --> 00:02:22.767
And think of him frozen in time

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:23.810
as forever

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:24.769
that person

00:02:24.769 --> 00:02:27.188
for those incredible ten seasons.

00:02:27.564 --> 00:02:29.774
You know, Perry and his costars

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:30.942
and they wrote about

00:02:30.942 --> 00:02:33.278
they were more than just cast mates.

00:02:33.278 --> 00:02:35.113
They were a family.

00:02:35.113 --> 00:02:36.364
And in fact

00:02:36.406 --> 00:02:36.948
here he is

00:02:36.948 --> 00:02:39.909
reflecting on their bond back in HBO.

00:02:39.909 --> 00:02:41.911
Max's really

00:02:41.911 --> 00:02:44.706
highly anticipated and beloved 2021

00:02:44.706 --> 00:02:46.416
friends reunion special. Listen

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.211
the best way that I can describe

00:02:50.211 --> 00:02:54.174
it is after the show was over at a party

00:02:54.215 --> 00:02:56.634
or any any kind of social gathering.

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:59.137
If one of us bumped into each other,

00:02:59.137 --> 00:02:59.679
that was it.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.014
That was the end of the night.

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:02.765
You just sat with the side

00:03:02.765 --> 00:03:05.226
with the person all night long.

00:03:05.435 --> 00:03:07.812
I remember that was it

00:03:07.812 --> 00:03:08.730
you apologize

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.273
to the people you were with,

00:03:10.273 --> 00:03:11.941
but they had to understand

00:03:11.941 --> 00:03:14.152
you had met somebody special to you

00:03:14.152 --> 00:03:15.570
and you were going to talk to that person

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:17.322
for the rest of the night.

00:03:18.281 --> 00:03:19.991
I mean, talk to us about that bond

00:03:19.991 --> 00:03:22.410
and really how it also translated

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.454
to the need to protect one another

00:03:24.454 --> 00:03:26.664
and to protect Matthew

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:29.375
Well,

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.126
you know,

00:03:30.168 --> 00:03:32.462
the cast for every episode

00:03:32.462 --> 00:03:33.880
from the very beginning

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.465
would gather backstage

00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:36.758
and they would huddle

00:03:36.758 --> 00:03:38.384
before they would go out.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:41.596
And so and then they would,

00:03:41.804 --> 00:03:43.348
you know, gathered during the day

00:03:43.348 --> 00:03:44.641
in between rehearsal

00:03:44.641 --> 00:03:45.975
and the lunches together.

00:03:45.975 --> 00:03:48.478
So it really was a family

00:03:48.478 --> 00:03:49.938
kind of situation.

00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:52.440
And I think, you know, with

00:03:52.941 --> 00:03:54.609
Matthew, with all of his

00:03:54.609 --> 00:03:56.694
his troubles over the years,

00:03:56.694 --> 00:03:58.238
I think this cast really,

00:03:59.656 --> 00:04:00.698
you know, supported him

00:04:00.698 --> 00:04:01.157
in a way

00:04:01.157 --> 00:04:02.492
that allowed him

00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:04.661
to be the comic genius that he was.

00:04:04.953 --> 00:04:05.286
I think

00:04:05.286 --> 00:04:07.747
without that perfect cast around him,

00:04:07.956 --> 00:04:08.331
you know,

00:04:08.331 --> 00:04:10.124
it could've been a different story.

00:04:10.124 --> 00:04:12.585
But I also, you know,

00:04:12.961 --> 00:04:15.838
his relationship with Joey,

00:04:15.838 --> 00:04:16.631
you know, the

00:04:16.631 --> 00:04:17.590
Chandler and Joey,

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:20.426
I think Lou is something very special

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.220
that we hadn't seen before in TV.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.681
They were like the odd couple next door

00:04:25.306 --> 00:04:26.432
and

00:04:28.893 --> 00:04:29.435
yeah.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:32.981
So I mean, the magic of that show

00:04:32.981 --> 00:04:34.315
and I have to tell you,

00:04:34.315 --> 00:04:36.442
sometimes people have the misimpression

00:04:36.818 --> 00:04:38.945
that those who are in comedy

00:04:39.737 --> 00:04:41.197
either are not as talented

00:04:41.197 --> 00:04:43.032
or as great of an actor or artist,

00:04:43.032 --> 00:04:43.825
they think that comedy

00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:45.618
somehow is a lesser form

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:46.327
and certainly not.

00:04:46.327 --> 00:04:47.453
It's one of the hardest things

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:48.997
to pull off

00:04:48.997 --> 00:04:49.622
to land

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:50.248
the lines

00:04:50.248 --> 00:04:51.332
time after time,

00:04:51.332 --> 00:04:52.292
night after night,

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.126
in a way

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.752
that makes people relate to them

00:04:54.752 --> 00:04:56.796
in such a way and deliver

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.298
some of the most iconic moments

00:04:58.298 --> 00:04:59.841
of this beloved show.

00:05:01.092 --> 00:05:01.843
And yet,

00:05:01.843 --> 00:05:05.096
what a contrast to this beautiful, raw,

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:07.140
vulnerable memoir

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.016
that he released,

00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:09.100
where he really talks

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:12.979
about just how vulnerable he really was.

00:05:13.271 --> 00:05:14.647
Were you aware at the time

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:15.690
when all this was going to that

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:17.025
those were the struggles

00:05:17.025 --> 00:05:17.984
that he was facing?

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:20.028
And if so, were you surprised

00:05:20.028 --> 00:05:22.363
that he shared them with the world

00:05:24.532 --> 00:05:25.783
We were aware

00:05:25.783 --> 00:05:28.494
that he was facing personal struggles

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:30.496
and there were times

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.832
where he had to leave the show

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:36.044
for several months to go to rehab.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:37.754
But,

00:05:38.588 --> 00:05:39.672
you know, in general,

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:42.216
I think that the show supported him

00:05:42.216 --> 00:05:45.219
in a way for those years and,

00:05:46.929 --> 00:05:49.599
you know, just allowed him to

00:05:51.976 --> 00:05:53.728
be in the struggle.

00:05:53.728 --> 00:05:54.729
You know,

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:56.022
you know,

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:57.482
he has been using this platform

00:05:57.482 --> 00:05:59.901
and he had been using his platform

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:02.111
to really be

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:03.821
a guiding light,

00:06:03.821 --> 00:06:05.448
to be a force of influence

00:06:05.448 --> 00:06:06.741
for so many people

00:06:06.741 --> 00:06:08.284
who are battling addiction.

00:06:08.284 --> 00:06:11.287
But also saw him as one of them,

00:06:11.287 --> 00:06:12.914
which made it all the more powerful.

00:06:12.914 --> 00:06:13.122
You know,

00:06:13.122 --> 00:06:13.915
he had a choice

00:06:13.915 --> 00:06:16.000
and he chose to use his platform.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.336
There are so many iconic moments.

00:06:18.336 --> 00:06:19.128
I'm sure you've been watching

00:06:19.128 --> 00:06:19.879
social media

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:20.880
and seeing that people

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:21.255
have been

00:06:21.255 --> 00:06:22.965
sharing all their favorite either

00:06:22.965 --> 00:06:24.342
Chandler Bing lines

00:06:24.342 --> 00:06:26.010
or moments that they love.

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:27.053
I want to share for the audience

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:28.596
one of your favorites

00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:34.644
You make me happier

00:06:34.644 --> 00:06:38.231
than I ever thought I could be.

00:06:39.857 --> 00:06:41.901
And if you let me,

00:06:42.527 --> 00:06:44.028
I will spend the rest of my life

00:06:44.028 --> 00:06:47.115
trying to make you feel the same way.

00:06:55.665 --> 00:06:56.707
Monica

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:01.295
when your marriage

00:07:07.927 --> 00:07:09.637
at that moment

00:07:09.637 --> 00:07:11.806
still makes you smile, why

00:07:15.435 --> 00:07:16.519
Well, because, you know,

00:07:16.519 --> 00:07:18.938
we were rooting for Monica and Chandler

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:19.647
all along.

00:07:19.647 --> 00:07:21.190
I think that was the thing

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:23.401
about their relationship

00:07:23.401 --> 00:07:25.903
I remember when we were in London and

00:07:26.529 --> 00:07:28.156
we did the London wedding

00:07:28.156 --> 00:07:29.866
and we revealed the relationship

00:07:29.866 --> 00:07:31.576
to the first time

00:07:31.576 --> 00:07:32.535
Matthew and Courteney

00:07:32.535 --> 00:07:33.995
came out from under those covers.

00:07:33.995 --> 00:07:36.456
It was just like gangbusters.

00:07:36.456 --> 00:07:38.875
4 minutes in that place.

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:41.377
Just the applause would not stop.

00:07:42.545 --> 00:07:42.879
Wow.

00:07:42.879 --> 00:07:43.754
Well,

00:07:43.838 --> 00:07:46.716
a testament to the actor who was there.

00:07:46.716 --> 00:07:48.718
And even to this day, Kevin Bright,

00:07:48.718 --> 00:07:50.386
the applause does not stop

00:07:50.386 --> 00:07:51.554
for Matthew Perry.

00:07:51.554 --> 00:07:52.597
Thank you for sharing a little

00:07:52.597 --> 00:07:53.306
bit with us tonight.

00:07:55.224 --> 00:07:56.851
Thank you, Laura.

00:07:57.685 --> 00:07:58.394
We'll be right back.

